  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The unbiased die is thrown&nbsp;five times such that the product of the outcomes is positive,&nbsp;then either all outcomes are positive or any two are negative.</p><p>Either all outcomes are positive or any two are negative.</p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;(positive)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math> (negative) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Required probability</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>521</mn><mn>2592</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
